    <item>
      <author>Daniel Ren</author>
      <dc:creator>Daniel Ren</dc:creator>
      <description>Hesai Group, the world’s largest maker of lidar sensors for vehicles, has launched a 3D spatial camera as it expands into physical artificial intelligence in search of new growth opportunities.
The handheld device, called Kosmo, is described by Hesai as a “physical AI eye” and converts real-world environments into detailed, editable 3D models. The company said it was designed to standardise the digitisation of complex spaces such as campuses and factories.
“Our interesting new products, which...</description>
