    <item>
      <author>Daniel Ren</author>
      <dc:creator>Daniel Ren</dc:creator>
      <description>China’s electric vehicle (EV) makers have been hit with a double blow as both Beijing and Brussels introduce measures that will affect their exports, leading analysts to revise down their earnings forecasts for the industry.
The twin measures – combined with a sales decline in China’s domestic market – could create a “do-or-die moment” for some of the country’s 50-odd EV makers, ramping up financial pressure on the companies, according to industry officials.
On Friday, China and the European...</description>
