    <item>
      <author>Zhu Wenqian</author>
      <dc:creator>Zhu Wenqian</dc:creator>
      <description>LVMH, the world’s largest luxury goods group, has attributed an Asia sales drop in the third quarter – the only regional decline the company reported – to, in part, a slowdown in Chinese demand.
The Louis Vuitton, Dior, Bulgari and Fendi parent group said Asia took a hit from a sharp macro-led deterioration in Chinese consumer sentiment, with tangible impact on discretionary expenses, the group said during an earnings call session on Monday.
The fall in demand coincided with a string of...</description>
